WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:23.189 align:start position:0%
 
bye  today these men soldiers of a free  country  are leaving to fight today our  battlefield is the world  our transports our freighters go to the  furthest  islands of the earth  men of the united nations are landing  everywhere  soldiers from new york and chicago are  moving up to fight in the empty desert  to fight on battlefields of snow  and in the jungle men from the little  towns of montana  moving up in the heat of asia africa the  caribbean  their job is fighting they must be kept  safe  against disease against the special  dangers of the jungle  behind our men stand scientists of the  western hemisphere  these doctors are good neighbors from  two american countries  the united states and the republic of  colombia  here were their first battles their  weapons the test tube  the sterilized needle between the  equator and the panama canal  they fought their silent war their enemy  was hidden in the green branches of the  jungle  here the heat of the sky pours down 12  hours a day  there is no autumn no spring only months  of heat  and months of rain life is quick and  abundant and death is also abundant  here was the home of jungle yellow fever  a man who came here to work  or to fight on these dark trails was  condemned to grow sick  delirious eyes and skin turning yellow  before he died  a disease of young men of those who  built a house  or a camp in the infected forest  death waited for them in the heat of the  valleys wooden crosses for the young men  who dared to walk in the jungle  they died from the bite of a mosquito  in a few laboratories they put this  disease behind glass and studied it  it was a virus it had to be fed on  living tissue  on unborn chicks and human blood serum  it was dangerous invisible had killed  men who worked with it  what they needed was a vaccine to  prevent yellow fever  and the fight never stopped till it was  found till it was tested  purified till it could be dried and  frozen  and prepared in quantity until it could  be transported  the first battle had been won inside the  white walls of a laboratory  the second battle was here in the heat  and wet of the jungle  above their heads was the solution to  the mystery of jungle yellow fever  the guilty mosquitoes lived and bred not  in pools on the ground  but in the treetops  they bit not only men but animals  especially monkeys  and thousands of monkeys grew sick but  did not die  their blood was a living reservoir of  yellow fever  mosquitoes which had fed on these  monkeys flew down from the treetops  attacked men and infected them with a  virus of yellow fever  to ride on these trails became a  sentence of death  but carried in this thermos jug too  precious to go on mule back  are tubes of vaccine packed in ice  moving over narrow trails and slippery  bridges  in a jungle area without railroads  without highways  across rivers too steep for navigation  at night they set up their portable  refrigerator unit  to renew the supply of ice in the  morning  it is carried on mule back with the  needles and syringes  a task force against yellow fever  there's a gray hot sunday in the town of  copair  there's market day too and there is good  news  yes it is true the doctors are coming  sunday mass is just over and in front of  the church  the news spreads it is true it is  printed  it is signed by the mayor the priest  himself has given his blessing  it has come at last  now the slow pack train climbs up the  hill from the jungle  the doctors have come to the town of  gopher  the every amarilla the yellow fever  the fever that eats men that kills their  fathers  their brothers the fever of the jungle  is to be  feared no longer the blessed medicine  has come  years of difficult work years of  collaboration between men of the united  states  cuba panama brazil colombia years of  courage in the laboratory and in the  jungle  come to their climax here in this patio  of the mayor's house  the vaccination will be here in the open  air  it is a dull cloudy afternoon 200 miles  north of the equator  the vaccine is removed from the thermos  jug  the instruments are sterilized in  boiling water  there are people here who read slowly  others who have never learned  but there's one word they know nacion  vaccination that word means life  and they know one thing more that if  three are sick with yellow fever  two will surely die and only one will  live  the names of the people are written down  the harness maker's wife  a farmer and his son  a woman is the first to be vaccinated  and now two more  these are a mixed people descendants of  indians  and of the spanish conquerors  a few drops of vaccine injected under  the skin of the arm  will give them dependable and lasting  immunity  those whose names are in this book need  have no fear of yellow fever  there is only one shock there is no  illness afterwards  the protection lasts for years perhaps  for life  it is a product of the genius of the  combined americas  already 500 000 citizens of colombia  have been vaccinated  now the vaccine is taken to army  hospitals where the entire colombian  army  unit by unit is vaccinated against  yellow fever  now they can go safely to their outposts  in the jungle  these soldiers are safe and because of  this pioneering work  when our heavy guns are lifted in the  jungle the men behind them will be  strong  ready to fight in the african congo on  the dark islands of the south pacific  in the jungles of burma and the solomons  in the depths of new guinea  and the philippines when we come to take  them one by one  our men today are safe against yellow  fever  free to fight the worst disease of all  fascism until that too shall be blasted  from the face of the earth  you

